# Format: [source] [destination] [code]. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Always point the destination at the EXTENSIONLESS form. Cloudflare Pages
# redirects every /foo.html to /foo before serving it — "Pages will also
# redirect HTML pages to their extension-less counterparts"
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/serving-pages/) — so a
# destination ending in .html costs the visitor and the crawler a second hop
# and dilutes the 301's signal across two URLs.
#
# Sources still need both forms. _redirects is evaluated before that automatic
# 308, so an .html source does match (verified live: /symptom-is-a-signal.html
# returned our 301, not the platform's 308). But the extensionless form was
# the URL that actually served 200 back when the page existed, so it is the
# one most likely to be linked, and it does not match an .html source rule.
#
# Careful: "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an
# asset matches the incoming request"
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/). A rule here will
# shadow a real page at the same path. Before adding a page whose slug appears
# below, delete the rule in the same change.

